<%# locals: (dom_id:, progress:, label: "CI", test_id: "ci-progress-bar", compact: false, wrapper_class: nil, inner_test_id: nil, href: nil, link_title: nil) %>
<%#
  Stable-id wrapper around the CI meter so a LIVE CI update (CiCheckJob
  after_commit, via DeploymentsBroadcaster) can morph-replace THIS slot alone — the
  meter re-renders, the surrounding card never flashes.

  Composes the meter inside a distinct OUTLINED CARD (a bordered panel within the
  task card): the "CI" label, the per-check icons (few checks) OR the "X / Y"
  fraction (many), and the state-coloured bar. A small suite (progress.symbolic?)
  shows the symbols row AND the shared track together; a large one shows the numeric
  bar. Both render the track, so the bar is always visible.

  When `href` is present the whole card becomes a link that opens in a NEW TAB
  (target=_blank rel=noopener); @click.stop keeps the card's own click-to-open-task
  handler from firing. Two callers pass one: the task card links its devops.pr_url,
  the Next Release G3 track links that repo's Actions run (release_ci_run_url).
  `link_title` names the destination for the anchor's title + aria-label (the link's
  accessible name) — it defaults to the PR wording. Absent href (no run/PR resolved)
  -> a plain panel, no link, never a broken href="#".

  The outer div ALWAYS renders (even when blank) so the Turbo replace target exists
  before the run's first check settles; empty, it is a zero-height block.
%>
<div id="<%= dom_id %>" data-test="<%= dom_id %>-slot">
  <% if progress.respond_to?(:present?) && progress.present? %>
    <% meter = capture do %>
      <% if progress.symbolic? %>
        <%= render "components/ci_progress_symbols",
              progress: progress, label: (label || "CI"), test_id: test_id, compact: compact %>
        <%= render "components/ci_progress_track",
              progress: progress, test_id: test_id, compact: compact %>
      <% else %>
        <%= render "components/ci_progress_bar",
              progress: progress, label: (label || "CI"), test_id: test_id, compact: compact %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>
    <%# The CI-METER VARIANT of the shared components/_card_bar shell — the SAME
        card_bar_base_classes geometry (w-full rounded border px-2 py-1) the status /
        CTA / blocker bars use, so the meter lines up as a coherent sibling in the
        stack; its two content rows just make it a touch taller. Own tone: a subtle
        inset panel. When a run/PR resolved, the whole panel is a new-tab link with a
        three-state hover ladder (default bg-inset/50 -> group-hover:bg-inset/75 while
        the PARENT card is hovered -> hover:!bg-inset on direct hover; ! beats the
        group rule). Absent href -> a plain panel, never a broken href="#". %>
    <% link_label = link_title.presence || "Open the pull request on GitHub" %>
    <%= render "components/card_bar",
          body: meter,
          class_extra: "ci-progress-card block space-y-1 border-subtle bg-inset/50 transition-colors #{wrapper_class}",
          link_class_extra: "group-hover:bg-inset/75 hover:!bg-inset hover:border-primary/40",
          href: href.presence, new_tab: true,
          test_id: inner_test_id,
          title: (link_label if href.present?),
          aria_label: (link_label if href.present?) %>
  <% end %>
</div>
